(6980124, 1047983, 117474, '<td valign="top">A little late... but better late than never, right? <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1000203" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1000203.gif'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1000203.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1000203.gif"/></a></td>', 'A little late... but better late than never, right? ', '2013-02-16 07:37:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(6985297, 1048798, 138630, '<td valign="top">You may or may not be aware that this is one of the photos being used in the online "publications" referenced here: <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1188924" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">DPC forum thread on LBNelert</a> <br/>I noticed it when I was searching for my own. There were so many from DPC that I could not document them all - if you want to have it removed, see posts from LydiaToo and Mike_311 on p. 5 of the forum thread. To locate it more easily, check both blogs and the main newsletter, starting with the dates when this challenge was in voting or shortly thereafter.</td>', 'You may or may not be aware that this is one of the photos being used in the online "publications" referenced here: DPC forum thread on LBNelert I noticed it when I was searching for my own. There were so many from DPC that I could not document them all - if you want to have it removed, see posts from LydiaToo and Mike_311 on p. 5 of the forum thread. To locate it more easily, check both blogs and the main newsletter, starting with the dates when this challenge was in voting or shortly thereafter.', '2013-02-24 15:03:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(6988980, 1048275, 67258, '<td valign="top">Stefan, you asked for some feedback on your entries, so hope here goes!<br/> <br/>I gave this a 5.  The positives - the entry met the challenge well; the composition has been carefully considered and is good, with an aesthetically pleasing symmetry.  I was less convinced by the ''authenticity'' of the shot - bits just didn''t quite ring true, the very dirty boots, but well manicured nails, clean hands and cardboard sign.  For me, though, the biggest drawback of the image was the style of processing.  I note that some commenters admired the textures in your photo, but I feel your choice of processing diminished them.  <br/> <br/>Hope this helps!</td>', 'Stefan, you asked for some feedback on your entries, so hope here goes! I gave this a 5.  The positives - the entry met the challenge well; the composition has been carefully considered and is good, with an aesthetically pleasing symmetry.  I was less convinced by the ''authenticity'' of the shot - bits just didn''t quite ring true, the very dirty boots, but well manicured nails, clean hands and cardboard sign.  For me, though, the biggest drawback of the image was the style of processing.  I note that some commenters admired the textures in your photo, but I feel your choice of processing diminished them.   Hope this helps!', '2013-03-01 17:07:45.000000', NULL, 0);
COMMIT;
